            "review_title": "Review at The Crab Shack Thao Dien",
            "review_text": "Ngọc Anh N\n3 contributions\n0\nGreat for Dates\nJan 2025 • Couples\nThis branch has a completely different vibe to Tu Xuong, it's smaller, cozier, and perfect for a dinner date. The atmosphere feels warm and relaxed, and the staff here are especially friendly and attentive. As for the food, everything is consistently fresh, from shrimp to huge crabs. Both the Cajun and orange sauces are excellent, but the Cajun really stands out if you enjoy spicy, rich flavors. What surprised me most was the noodle dish—simple but so flavorful that it’s now something I always order. Another dish that shouldn’t be missed is the crab cheese oven specialty, which tastes amazing when eaten with bread. This branch also lets you choose your own live lobster or king crab, adding a fun experience to the meal. Even though the price is on the higher side, the quality and the cozy, romantic vibe make it absolutely worth visiting.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 3, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
